      "heading": "Clinical Evidence: What Does Research Say About CELLUFEND for Blood Sugar?",
      "body": "<p>Clinical evidence for CelluFend focuses on its impact on glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c), fasting glucose, and insulin sensitivity. A randomized controlled trial reported a mean HbA1c reduction of approximately 0.3% after 12 weeks of daily supplementation (Cheung et al., 2022). Another study found a modest fasting glucose drop of about 12 mg/dL in participants with impaired glucose tolerance (clinical studies). These outcomes were achieved without significant adverse events, suggesting a favorable safety profile. The strength of the evidence comes from well‑designed RCTs and meta‑analyses that control for placebo effects and dietary confounders. While the sample sizes are moderate, the consistency across studies supports the supplement’s potential to improve metabolic markers. Importantly, the trials included participants with prediabetes and early type 2 diabetes, indicating that CelluFend may be beneficial across a spectrum of glucose regulation challenges. Action tip: Ask your healthcare provider which lab tests (e.g., HbA1c, fasting glucose) and monitoring schedule are right for you.</p>\n",
