      "heading": "Dosage and How to Use Cellufend for Type 2 Diabetes for Blood Sugar",
      "body": "<p>The recommended approach for most users is to start with a lower dose and gradually increase as tolerated. A typical progression might involve: <strong>Recommended Daily Schedule</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"md-table\"><thead><tr><th class=\"tbl-th\">Week</th><th class=\"tbl-th\">Focus</th><th class=\"tbl-th\">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">1</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Start low</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Take 500 mg with breakfast</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">2</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Assess tolerance</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Increase to 750 mg if no GI upset</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">3</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Maintain</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Continue 750 mg daily</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">4</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Optional increase</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Add 250 mg to reach 1000 mg if desired</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"tbl-source\">Source: Cheung et al., 2022</p>\n<p>The supplement should be taken with a regular meal to promote consistent absorption and reduce gastrointestinal discomfort. Taking CelluFend with a meal enhances the bioavailability of its active constituents—primarily the polysaccharide complex derived from <em>Cellulophaga</em> species—by providing a steady pH environment and a reservoir of digestive enzymes that facilitate mucosal penetration. This timing also synchronizes the peak plasma concentration with the post‑prandial glucose surge, allowing the active compounds to exert their modulatory effects on insulin sensitivity and hepatic gluconeogenesis during the critical window when blood glucose rises.</p>\n<p>If you experience mild nausea or diarrhea, consider taking the dose with a larger portion of food or splitting the dose into two smaller servings. Splitting the dose can mitigate transient gastrointestinal irritation by reducing the instantaneous load on the gut mucosa, while a larger meal provides additional dietary fiber that may synergize with CelluFend’s prebiotic action, fostering a healthier gut microbiome that has been linked to improved glycemic control.</p>\n<p>Always follow the product label for exact dosing instructions and consult a healthcare provider before making changes, especially if you are on diabetes medication. This precaution is essential because CelluFend’s glucose‑lowering effects could potentiate the action of insulin or sulfonylureas, increasing the risk of hypoglycemia. A clinician can adjust medication dosages or recommend monitoring strategies such as more frequent capillary glucose checks during the titration period.</p>\n<p>Action tip: Take with a regular meal to build a consistent daily habit. Consistency not only improves absorption but also reinforces behavioral adherence, which is a critical determinant of long‑term metabolic benefit.</p>\n",
